{# #### `project_attributes_setting_outbound_max_active_calls` #}

{{SetCustomerMetadataAttribute(
    idn="project_attributes_setting_outbound_max_active_calls",
    field="multiple_fields",
    value={ "title": "Outbound - Max Active Calls [C]", "description": """This advanced setting defines the maximum number of outbound calls that can run at the same time.

It protects throughput stability by limiting concurrent call load and avoiding connector
oversubscription.

**Best Practice:** Align this value with your voice provider capacity, account limits, and
acceptable queue latency.

Behavior:

- **Below limit:** New tasks launch immediately.
- **At limit:** New tasks are queued and started automatically when active slots are freed.

---

**⚙️ Technical & System Details (Advanced)**

**System Usage:** Before starting a call, runtime checks active call count and compares it with this
limit. Active calls are tracked in AKB entries labeled `active_call`; queued tasks are stored in an
AKB queue record (`queued_calls`). Active-call records are kept idempotent by task ID, and queue
records are de-duplicated by task ID. On call completion/failure cleanup, the system attempts to
start the next queued task if capacity is available. If the voice provider rejects a launched
`make_call` because a call limit was reached, runtime releases the active-call record and moves the
task into retry handling instead of leaving it in active-call tracking.

**Fallbacks:** If empty, initialization seeds `50`, and runtime guards also use default `50` in
capacity checks.

**Dependencies:**

- **Primary Settings:**
  - `project_attributes_setting_outbound_naive_conversation_deadline_seconds`: Influences how long a
    call may hold a concurrency slot before deadline-based failure handling releases capacity.
- **Logic Interactions:**
  - `task_manager_dispatch_task`: Internal worker handoff where capacity is checked before launch.
  - `outbound_call_finished`: Completion path that releases active-call tracking and triggers queued
    call startup.""", "group": "Module - Outbound", "value_type": "number", "is_hidden": True }
)}}

{# #### `project_attributes_setting_outbound_naive_conversation_deadline_seconds` #}

{{SetCustomerMetadataAttribute(
    idn="project_attributes_setting_outbound_naive_conversation_deadline_seconds",
    field="multiple_fields",
    value={ "title": "Outbound - Conversation Start Deadline (Queue Timeout) [C]", "description": """This advanced setting defines how many seconds the system waits for a call to actually start after
an outbound call attempt is launched.

If the conversation does not start in time, the deadline timer closes the attempt with a deadline
reason and the dispatcher moves into outbound completion analysis.

**Best Practice:** Set this high enough to tolerate provider setup latency, but low enough to avoid
holding capacity slots for stalled attempts.

Behavior:

- **Within deadline:** When call start is confirmed, the deadline timer is canceled and normal call
  flow continues.
- **Deadline exceeded:** The dispatcher closes the active attempt, frees the outbound slot, and
  starts the conversation-retrieval/analyzing path for follow-up handling.

---

**⚙️ Technical & System Details (Advanced)**

**System Usage:** Outbound call launch sets a `call_deadline_exceeded` timer on `outbound_timer`
using this value. The `conversation_started` event disables that timer. `make_call` startup error
handling also disables the same timer so a failed startup cannot later produce a stale deadline
failure for the task. If the timer fires, runtime emits `outbound_call_finished` with deadline
reason, increments attempt count, removes the active call from tracking, starts queued-call release
logic, and requests conversation retrieval while the task moves to `analyzing`.

**Fallbacks:** If empty, initialization seeds `180`, and call launch logic also guards with default
`180`.

**Dependencies:**

- **Primary Settings:**
  - `project_attributes_setting_outbound_max_active_calls`: Capacity slot pressure and queue release
    behavior are affected by how long attempts wait before deadline failure.
- **Logic Interactions:**
  - `call_deadline_exceeded`: Timer event fired when the start deadline is exceeded.
  - `conversation_started`: Cancels the deadline timer.
  - `outbound_call_finished`: Consolidates deadline failures into shared outbound completion logic.
  - `project_attributes_setting_outbound_default_retry_number`: Can affect later retry handling if
    conversation retrieval returns empty after deadline completion.""", "group": "Module - Outbound", "value_type": "number", "is_hidden": True }
)}}

{# #### `project_attributes_setting_outbound_payload_schema` #}

{{SetCustomerMetadataAttribute(
    idn="project_attributes_setting_outbound_payload_schema",
    field="multiple_fields",
    value={ "title": "Outbound - Payload Schema [C]", "description": """This advanced setting defines a JSON schema for extra fields that should be extracted from outbound
conversation content before sending result payloads.

Use it to enrich outbound callbacks with structured data (for example intent tags or custom business
fields) derived from call/SMS conversation text.

**Best Practice:** Keep this as a valid JSON schema object with explicit field descriptions and
types. Fields that cannot be reliably extracted are returned as `null`.

**Examples:**

```json
{
  \"type\": \"object\",
  \"properties\": {
    \"lead_interest\": {
      \"type\": \"string\",
      \"description\": \"Short summary of user interest level.\"
    },
    \"follow_up_priority\": {
      \"type\": \"string\",
      \"description\": \"Priority label: high, medium, or low.\"
    }
  }
}
```

---

**⚙️ Technical & System Details (Advanced)**

**System Usage:** After outbound conversation analysis, runtime builds a base payload and, when this
schema is non-empty, runs structured extraction against conversation transcript/memory. Extracted
fields are merged into the outgoing payload before endpoint dispatch.

**Fallbacks:** If empty during initialization, this attribute is seeded with `{}`. Blank or `{}` at
runtime disables schema-based enrichment and sends only the base payload fields.

**Dependencies:**

- **Primary Settings:**
  - `project_attributes_setting_outbound_request_endpoint`: Controls whether enriched payloads are
    actually delivered externally.
  - `project_attributes_setting_outbound_request_headers`: Applied as HTTP headers when dispatching
    enriched payloads.
- **Logic Interactions:**
  - `convoagent_conversation_retrieved`: Call conversation analysis path that can apply this schema.
  - `custom_session_ended`: SMS analysis path that can apply this schema.""", "group": "Module - Outbound", "value_type": "json", "is_hidden": True }
)}}

{# #### `project_attributes_setting_outbound_request_endpoint` #}

{{SetCustomerMetadataAttribute(
    idn="project_attributes_setting_outbound_request_endpoint",
    field="multiple_fields",
    value={ "title": "Outbound - Request Endpoint [C]", "description": """This advanced setting defines the HTTP endpoint URL that receives outbound result payloads.

When configured, payload delivery is attempted for outbound call and outbound SMS result flows.

**Best Practice:** Use a stable HTTPS endpoint with request logging and idempotent processing.

Behavior:

- **Endpoint is set:** The system posts outbound result payloads (finished/failed/error paths) to
  this URL.
- **Endpoint is empty:** External POST requests are skipped; internal task updates and result
  recording continue.

**Examples:**

```txt
https://api.example.com/outbound/callback
```

---

**⚙️ Technical & System Details (Advanced)**

**System Usage:** Before dispatch, runtime enriches payload with core identifiers (`phone_number`,
`user_id`, `task_id`) and merges optional callback arguments from task context. It then sends a POST
request via `http_connector` using `project_attributes_setting_outbound_request_headers`.

**Fallbacks:** If empty during initialization, this attribute is set to an empty string. At runtime,
empty value short-circuits webhook sending logic.

**Dependencies:**

- **Primary Settings:**
  - `project_attributes_setting_outbound_request_headers`: Header JSON used for outbound HTTP POST.
  - `project_attributes_setting_outbound_payload_schema`: Optional enrichment schema for payload
    content before dispatch.
- **Logic Interactions:**
  - `convoagent_conversation_retrieved`: Call-analysis route that can trigger endpoint dispatch.
  - `custom_session_ended`: SMS-analysis route that can trigger endpoint dispatch.
  - `result_error`: Call error route that can trigger endpoint dispatch.
  - `server_message_error`: Additional call error route that can trigger endpoint dispatch through
    shared no-answer handling.
  - `send_sms_error`: SMS error route that can trigger endpoint dispatch.""", "group": "Module - Outbound", "value_type": "string", "is_hidden": True }
)}}

{# #### `project_attributes_setting_outbound_request_headers` #}

{{SetCustomerMetadataAttribute(
    idn="project_attributes_setting_outbound_request_headers",
    field="multiple_fields",
    value={ "title": "Outbound - Request Headers [C]", "description": """This advanced setting defines HTTP headers used when outbound result payloads are posted to your
external endpoint.

Use it to pass authentication and integration metadata (for example API keys, bearer tokens, or
tenant headers).

**Best Practice:** Provide a valid JSON object of headers and keep credential values rotated through
your standard secret-management process.

**Examples:**

```json
{
  \"Authorization\": \"Bearer <token>\",
  \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",
  \"X-Tenant-Id\": \"acme\"
}
```

---

**⚙️ Technical & System Details (Advanced)**

**System Usage:** When outbound webhook dispatch is active, these headers are passed directly to the
HTTP `send_request` command used for call and SMS result payload delivery.

**Fallbacks:** During initialization, blank value is normalized to empty string. At runtime, empty
value is converted to `{}` before request dispatch, so webhook sends continue without custom
headers.

**Dependencies:**

- **Primary Settings:**
  - `project_attributes_setting_outbound_request_endpoint`: Header configuration is applied only
    when endpoint dispatch is enabled.
- **Logic Interactions:**
  - `convoagent_conversation_retrieved`: Call-analysis route that can dispatch payloads with these
    headers.
  - `custom_session_ended`: SMS-analysis route that can dispatch payloads with these headers.
  - `result_error`: Call error route that can dispatch payloads with these headers.
  - `server_message_error`: Additional call error route that can dispatch payloads with these
    headers through shared no-answer handling.
  - `send_sms_error`: SMS error route that can dispatch payloads with these headers.""", "group": "Module - Outbound", "value_type": "json", "is_hidden": True }
)}}

{# #### `project_attributes_setting_outbound_sms_session_duration` #}

{{SetCustomerMetadataAttribute(
    idn="project_attributes_setting_outbound_sms_session_duration",
    field="multiple_fields",
    value={ "title": "Outbound SMS - Session Duration [C]", "description": """This advanced setting defines how many minutes an outbound SMS session stays open while waiting for
the user to respond.

Use it to control how long the system waits before concluding the SMS interaction window.

**Best Practice:** Set a duration that matches your expected response behavior. Longer windows give
users more time to reply, while shorter windows finalize outcomes faster.

Behavior:

- **Longer duration:** Session remains active longer before response analysis is finalized.
- **Shorter duration:** Session closes sooner and follow-up analysis runs earlier.

---

**⚙️ Technical & System Details (Advanced)**

**System Usage:** After sending outbound SMS, runtime emits `extend_session` with timeout equal to
this value converted from minutes to seconds. When the session later ends, SMS outbound analysis
(`custom_session_ended`) determines finished/failed outcome, updates records, and may dispatch
external payloads.

**Fallbacks:** If empty during initialization, this attribute defaults to `60`.

**Dependencies:**

- **Primary Settings:**
  - `project_attributes_setting_outbound_request_endpoint`: If configured, SMS analysis results
    after session timeout can be posted externally.
  - `project_attributes_setting_outbound_payload_schema`: Optional schema enrichment applied during
    SMS conversation analysis.
- **Logic Interactions:**
  - `extend_session`: Receives timeout derived from this setting.
  - `custom_session_ended`: Triggers outbound SMS result analysis after the session window closes.""", "group": "Module - Outbound", "value_type": "number", "is_hidden": True }
)}}

